 "text": [
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Numbers from seanome/2024-kmerseek-analysis at commit 7eca428b (results/leaderboard), copied 2026-10-20."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h1",
   "text": "Coverage"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "What has been measured, across every experiment in the tables, and what has not. Every empty square is a run still to do."
  },
  {
   "tag": "figcaption",
   "text": "Figure 2a. Tool by stratum axis. A filled square means the tables hold measured rows for that tool there. The number under it is the count of true instances scored, summed over experiments, query sets, relatives and truth sets. An empty square means not run."
  },
  {
   "tag": "figcaption",
   "text": "Figure 2b. Tool by experiment. A filled square means the tables hold measured rows for that tool there. The number under it is the count of true instances scored, summed over the query sets, relatives, truth sets and strata of that experiment. An empty square means not run. The last column, scope40_v040_shuffled_k2_seed1, is a null control for kmerseek (alphabet letters shuffled), not a run other tools need."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "111 squares are filled and 93 are empty. Where each experiment's output came from, and which outputs were left out and why: inventory.md (copied with the tables)."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "text": "What to run next"
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "text": "phmmer: experiment alphabet_ranking_three_cases; experiment dark_set_gain; experiment scope40_v040; experiment scope40_v040_below_kmin."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "text": "MMseqs2: experiment alphabet_ranking_three_cases; experiment dark_set_accuracy; experiment dark_set_gain; experiment dark_set_pfam_fmax; experiment deep_twilight; experiment scope40_v040; experiment scope40_v040_below_kmin."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "text": "jackhmmer: experiment alphabet_ranking_three_cases; experiment dark_set_gain; experiment deep_twilight; experiment scope40_v040; experiment scope40_v040_below_kmin."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "text": "MMseqs2, three rounds: experiment alphabet_ranking_three_cases; experiment dark_set_accuracy; experiment dark_set_gain; experiment dark_set_pfam_fmax; experiment deep_twilight; experiment scope40_v040; experiment scope40_v040_below_kmin."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "text": "HH-suite (hhsearch): experiment alphabet_ranking_three_cases; experiment dark_set_accuracy; experiment dark_set_gain; experiment dark_set_pfam_fmax; experiment deep_twilight; experiment scope40_v040; experiment scope40_v040_below_kmin."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "text": "Foldseek: experiment alphabet_ranking_three_cases; experiment dark_set_accuracy; experiment dark_set_gain; experiment dark_set_pfam_fmax; experiment scope40_v040; experiment scope40_v040_below_kmin."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "text": "ProstT5 + Foldseek: experiment alphabet_ranking_three_cases; experiment dark_set_accuracy; experiment dark_set_gain; experiment dark_set_pfam_fmax; experiment deep_twilight; experiment scope40_v040; experiment scope40_v040_below_kmin."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "text": "hmmscan with Pfam: % identity to nearest relative; Swiss-Prot feature type; experiment alphabet_ranking_three_cases; experiment dark_set_accuracy; experiment dark_set_gain; experiment dark_set_pfam_fmax; experiment deep_twilight; experiment elm_cover; experiment scope40_v040; experiment scope40_v040_below_kmin."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "text": "mmseqs2: % identity to nearest relative; AlphaFold pLDDT; Swiss-Prot feature type; region length; experiment alphabet_ranking_three_cases; experiment dark_set_gain; experiment elm_cover; experiment qfo_region_midi; experiment qfo_region_midi_plus; experiment qfo_region_mini; experiment scope40_v040; experiment scope40_v040_below_kmin."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "text": "folddisco: experiment alphabet_ranking_three_cases; experiment dark_set_accuracy; experiment dark_set_gain; experiment dark_set_pfam_fmax; experiment deep_twilight; experiment elm_cover; experiment qfo_region_midi_plus; experiment scope40_v040; experiment scope40_v040_below_kmin."
